<h2 id="frequently-asked-questions">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

<section class="faq" itemscope itemtype="https://schema.org/FAQPage">

<div itemscope itemprop="mainEntity" itemtype="https://schema.org/Question">
  <h3 itemprop="name">Can I still read books that are already on my old Kindle?</h3>
  <div itemscope itemprop="acceptedAnswer" itemtype="https://schema.org/Answer">
    <div itemprop="text">
      <p>Yes. Books already stored on the device are still readable. The cutoff only affects the device's ability to purchase new books and sync content from Amazon's cloud. However, if you ever delete a book from the device, you will not be able to re-download it from Amazon onto that specific device.</p>
    </div>
